    "answer": {
      "short": "$653\\,000$ deer.",
      "worked": "Separate variables and use the supplied partial fractions:\n$$\\begin{aligned}\n\\int\\left(\\frac1P+\\frac1{C-P}\\right)\\,dP&=\\int0.1\\,dt\\\\\n\\ln|P|-\\ln|C-P|&=0.1t+k\\\\\n\\frac{P}{C-P}&=Ae^{0.1t}.\n\\end{aligned}$$\nAt $t=0$, $P=200\\,000$; at $t=20$, $P=500\\,000$:\n$$\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{200\\,000}{C-200\\,000}&=A\\\\\n\\frac{500\\,000}{C-500\\,000}&=Ae^2.\n\\end{aligned}$$\nDivide the second equation by the first:\n$$\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{5(C-200\\,000)}{2(C-500\\,000)}&=e^2\\\\\n5(C-200\\,000)&=2e^2(C-500\\,000)\\\\\n(2e^2-5)C&=1\\,000\\,000(e^2-1)\\\\\nC&=\\frac{1\\,000\\,000(e^2-1)}{2e^2-5}\\\\\nC&\\approx653\\,000.\n\\end{aligned}$$\nThe carrying capacity is $653\\,000$ deer, to the nearest thousand.",
